<p>All readings for this unit come from Aquinas's <em>Summa Theologiae</em>, First Part of the Second Part (Prima Secundae), in the Dominican Fathers translation. The text is in the public domain and free to read online. Each link below opens one Question.</p>
<ul>
<li><a href="https://www.newadvent.org/summa/2090.htm" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><strong>Question 90: Of the Essence of Law</strong></a> (4 articles) — What a law is</li>
<li><a href="https://www.newadvent.org/summa/2091.htm" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><strong>Question 91: Of the Various Kinds of Law</strong></a> (6 articles) — Eternal, natural, human, and divine law</li>
<li><a href="https://www.newadvent.org/summa/2094.htm" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><strong>Question 94: Of the Natural Law</strong></a> (6 articles) — The first precept, what natural law contains, and whether it can change</li>
<li><a href="https://www.newadvent.org/summa/2095.htm" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><strong>Question 95, Articles 1–2: Of Human Law</strong></a> — Whether human law is useful, and whether an unjust human law is really a law</li>
</ul>
